description: Glue / reconcile / sync helpers must document the compromise plainly
alwaysApply: true
---

# Document the smell

When you add **glue** because two machines disagree — reconcile, sync, “fix up after X”, pre-loop patches, dual null-checks — treat it as a **known smell**, not a clever helper.

## Before writing the body

Sketch the KDoc (or say it in chat): *why the honest owner cannot do this job*. If you cannot name that in one sentence, do not add the glue yet.

## Required on the method

- **Why not the honest place** — e.g. crank `while (!needsPlayerInput)` never enters SELECT/OFFER after takeAction nested a continuation
- **Real signal** — drive off domain shape (pending nest, stage), not a parallel field’s null (`currentPlayerAction != null`)
- **One case per branch** — prefer explicit arms over a boolean that returns `false` for three different reasons
- **Name empty / edge states** — e.g. “no pending on OFFER_* = Skip/Decline already cleared; arm advances next”

## Do not

- Soften the prose (“aligns”, “ensures”, “reconciles state”) — say what lies
- Hide the compromise in chat-only explanation; the next reader won’t have the thread
- Add a second glue layer to paper over the first without documenting both

Canonical example: `TurnEngine.reconcilePlayerActionStep`.
